{content}", "class_name": "Document", "text": "Manual Control works basically in the same way that RPM Control Mode does. The difference is that when the system is turned ON in manual mode the Set Point is set to the current engine speed. For example, if the Cruise Control is OFF and the engine speed is 2500 RPM, and the system is turned on, the engine will hold the engine speed at 2500 RPM.
