{"id_": "309ce7ee-4083-4e38-9bf3-efa6f4adb29e", "embedding": null, "metadata": {}, "excluded_embed_metadata_keys": [], "excluded_llm_metadata_keys": [], "relationships": {}, "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_separator": "
", "text_resource": {"embeddings": null, "text": "The throttle actuator control (TAC) system uses two pedal position (PP) sensors to monitor the pedal position. Two processors are also used to monitor the TAC system data. The engine control module (ECM) performs an intrusive test in order to detect that the PP signals are not shorted together. The ECM accomplishes this by pulling the PP sensor 2 low momentarily and looking for sensor 1 to also be low. The TAC system also performs this test on the throttle position (TP) sensors. This diagnostic monitors the transistor used to pull one pedal and one throttle sensor to ground simultaneously. Additionally, both processors monitor each other's data to verify that the indicated PP calculation is correct. If the transistor does not toggle within a calibrated period, or the indicated PP calculation is incorrect, SPN 65616, FMI 12 sets.
", "path": null, "url": null, "mimetype": null}, "image_resource": null, "audio_resource": null, "video_resource": null, "text_template": "{metadata_str}

{content}", "class_name": "Document", "text": "The throttle actuator control (TAC) system uses two pedal position (PP) sensors to monitor the pedal position. Two processors are also used to monitor the TAC system data. The engine control module (ECM) performs an intrusive test in order to detect that the PP signals are not shorted together. The ECM accomplishes this by pulling the PP sensor 2 low momentarily and looking for sensor 1 to also be low. The TAC system also performs this test on the throttle position (TP) sensors. This diagnostic monitors the transistor used to pull one pedal and one throttle sensor to ground simultaneously. Additionally, both processors monitor each other's data to verify that the indicated PP calculation is correct. If the transistor does not toggle within a calibrated period, or the indicated PP calculation is incorrect, SPN 65616, FMI 12 sets.
"}

